cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you reference this work, please cite it as below."
title: "Pre-action user-authorization conflict: causal tests of authorization representations"
abstract: >-
  A five-stage pre-registered interpretability study asking whether small
  open-weight chat models represent whether the user authorized the specific
  action they are about to take, and whether that representation is causally
  load-bearing for the decision. Authorization status is linearly decodable
  with held-out AUROC 1.00, but frozen-direction interventions produce
  statistically detectable and behaviorally negligible effects with zero
  decision flips.
authors:
